|~ `::link`, the kind of a link, and the laws declared under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [D114]. ~|

:link
  |~~ A link is a query a page names for its reader to follow to another
      page, written in the prose of a doc as a quote under this tag,
      `::link~(::vec | doc)`. Links make the pages a hypertext: a page
      names the pages that go deeper, and `open` runs the query a link
      holds, so `::qlang | doc | links | map ~open` answers the pages
      the first page names.

      A link opens a page, every link of the catalog among them; a query
      that lists or shows something is a snippet, and one that answers
      true a law. A host may stack its own tag over a link.
      ::snippet~(::qlang | doc | links) lists the links of the first page.
      ::link~(::snippet | doc) ::link~(::qlang/hypertext | doc)
  ~~|

:link/isALink
  |~~ A link a doc holds is a `::link`. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::link~(::qlang/values | doc) ~~| | links | first | type | eq ::link)

:link/opensToPages
  |~~ The links of the first page open to pages. ~~|
  ::law~(::qlang | doc | links | map ~open | every ~(type | eq ::doc))

:link/holdsUnderAStackOfTags
  |~~ A quote under a stack of tags holding `::link` is a link. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::Host::link~(1) ~~| | links | count | eq 1)
